       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum oral dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours would make the effects last. Normal kidney and liver function and the lack of allergies don't change this.\n\nCould this be a typo or a unit error? Here are some options:\n\n- **5 mg once daily** is the usual starting dose. It's often used for frail or elderly patients, or when starting therapy.\n- **10 mg once daily** is the maximum recommended dose.\n\nIf 50 mg is intended, for example because of a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Otherwise, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
